{
  "applied_operation_id": "op_c5c7fa2a7f2748329b6516d55f3b1d58",
  "claims": [
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_1c21cb6e16de6c98bffd03a5bacee83ebb995cd1367701fc65ecb8807dbbf5c3",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "specifications",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6",
          "git_sha": "792625886bdb1b62378aedbe9d2c13d0dda295d7",
          "line_end": 7,
          "line_start": 5,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "vivekhaldar/seed",
          "url": "https://github.com/vivekhaldar/seed/blob/cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6/README.md#L5-L7"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_c73d537d37cdadb3724e92bc9983b5148c2c7982b30387f913cab6f39e03ed4c"
      ],
      "text": "The README describes seed.py as calling a language model with a single exec tool that runs shell commands, loading its system prompt from self/SELF.md, with the agent able to edit self/ to retain tools, notes, and behavior between sessions."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_b0cd2e8c122e601bf592a9351e866f9f379e5e2c585889bc9ed34600889af803",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "tools-permissions",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6",
          "git_sha": "7a10c81129d8ecb30bdbfec61caaad632c7a2630",
          "line_end": 107,
          "line_start": 101,
          "path": "docs/DESIGN.md",
          "repository": "vivekhaldar/seed",
          "url": "https://github.com/vivekhaldar/seed/blob/cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6/docs/DESIGN.md#L101-L107"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_fb306a67e097e6df51102203cd5e22e867ee77a633e271f634ca15425271f637"
      ],
      "text": "The design doc states the one irreducible primitive is exec: the seed ships exactly one tool that runs a bash command and returns its output, with every other capability expressed through it rather than compressed further."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_7ccdf33d506a3508ca4925ede4604280a7f8cae461bb8f01c7a5879cbcb880ab",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "limitations",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6",
          "git_sha": "7a10c81129d8ecb30bdbfec61caaad632c7a2630",
          "line_end": 209,
          "line_start": 198,
          "path": "docs/DESIGN.md",
          "repository": "vivekhaldar/seed",
          "url": "https://github.com/vivekhaldar/seed/blob/cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6/docs/DESIGN.md#L198-L209"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_84b3bd16c8aac6c17cb92d151a14a4f0e6de8c00bad3a740cbd84bfb0b3bf70d"
      ],
      "text": "The risk register documents ungated exec as a consciously accepted risk: the agent runs arbitrary bash as the invoking user with no sandbox or approval gate, though every command and its output is printed to the terminal."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_caa1e9c43fbcf3d467be6d59e5648a07cfc0d73779707ab8f83efa73f16a1425",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "memory-state",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6",
          "git_sha": "792625886bdb1b62378aedbe9d2c13d0dda295d7",
          "line_end": 45,
          "line_start": 42,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "vivekhaldar/seed",
          "url": "https://github.com/vivekhaldar/seed/blob/cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6/README.md#L42-L45"
        },
        {
          "commit": "cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6",
          "git_sha": "7a10c81129d8ecb30bdbfec61caaad632c7a2630",
          "line_end": 132,
          "line_start": 127,
          "path": "docs/DESIGN.md",
          "repository": "vivekhaldar/seed",
          "url": "https://github.com/vivekhaldar/seed/blob/cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6/docs/DESIGN.md#L127-L132"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_803abcfa1c669721b5ae87c37a9167c8616676476519833c9bc616ea7ccd9012",
        "slc_9ff5c87d37d66bf1492de2dda29e2d19ad8e717e185fbe5a49fc00169508e1a7"
      ],
      "text": "Documentation states each session is fresh and its conversation is discarded on exit, so nothing survives except what the agent wrote into self/; a separate verbatim transcript is recorded per session as a flight recorder that is never loaded at boot."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_20cf0afd1bfc4fbfa799056a44053e60c1ad0c62da330a877eb445ace790d2ed",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "design-choices",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6",
          "git_sha": "7a10c81129d8ecb30bdbfec61caaad632c7a2630",
          "line_end": 125,
          "line_start": 116,
          "path": "docs/DESIGN.md",
          "repository": "vivekhaldar/seed",
          "url": "https://github.com/vivekhaldar/seed/blob/cd79a60acafe425f8bd31078996d5818bb151ad6/docs/DESIGN.md#L116-L125"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_99bda921e5574741d312ccd450aa931ffc3f6625a67a4fdebf1845a26b32b210"
      ],
      "text": "The design doc states the seed prompt and the agent's self-description were collapsed into the same mutable file: the loop's only hardcoded context decision is reading self/SELF.md, re-read every turn so self-edits take effect immediately."
    },
    {
