  "summary": "seed is documented as a minimal terminal coding agent: a single script calling a model with one exec tool, growing all further capability into a self/ directory the agent edits itself. Its design doc frames this as a deliberately auditable, ungated kernel with no sandbox, positioned against prior minimal-agent and self-improving-agent research. Evidence: all 3 of 3 candidate files stored (README.md, docs/DESIGN.md, SovereignLicense.md); selection complete.",
